# CrossEngin domain pack: comparative religion (v1)
#
# ~55 atoms + ~55 implications. Descriptive / comparative-religion
# content at academic-reference level (Britannica, Oxford Handbook of
# Religion, Cambridge History of Religions). Answers the vision's
# "religious analysis" call-out.
#
# EDITORIAL STANCE:
#   * Descriptive only. This pack states what traditions EXIST, what
#     they TEACH, and what their sacred texts + historical figures ARE
#     -- as documented by scholars of comparative religion. It makes NO
#     truth claims about theology, metaphysics, or the afterlife.
#   * Where scholarly consensus is strong (Christianity emerged in the
#     1st century CE), belief is high. Where scholarship debates
#     (exact date of Buddha's birth), belief is lower to reflect
#     genuine uncertainty.
#   * Cross-tradition claims ("prayer is a religious practice") get
#     FORMAL strength because they're ontological categorizations.
#     "Christianity teaches X" gets EMPIRICAL strength -- reflects
#     what a comparative-religion source SAYS, not a truth claim about
#     X itself.
#
# Ingest via:
#   /ingest cerec data/packs/religion.cerec religion \
#           src:pack:religion:v1

KG religion
SRC src:pack:religion:v1

# ============================================================================
# 1. Root ontology
# ============================================================================

ATOM religious_tradition 3 950
ATOM sacred_text 3 950
ATOM religious_practice 3 950
ATOM religious_leader 3 950
ATOM religious_holiday 3 950
ATOM sacred_place 3 950
ATOM person 3 950

IMP sacred_text religious_tradition EMPIRICAL

# ============================================================================
# 2. Major world religious traditions (Britannica, Pew Research)
# ============================================================================

ATOM christianity 3 1000
ATOM islam 3 1000
ATOM hinduism 3 1000
ATOM buddhism 3 1000
ATOM judaism 3 1000
ATOM sikhism 3 950
ATOM bahai_faith 3 900
ATOM zoroastrianism 3 900
ATOM jainism 3 900
ATOM shinto 3 900
ATOM taoism 3 900
ATOM indigenous_traditions 3 900

IMP christianity religious_tradition FORMAL
IMP islam religious_tradition FORMAL
IMP hinduism religious_tradition FORMAL
IMP buddhism religious_tradition FORMAL
IMP judaism religious_tradition FORMAL
IMP sikhism religious_tradition FORMAL
IMP bahai_faith religious_tradition FORMAL
IMP zoroastrianism religious_tradition FORMAL
IMP jainism religious_tradition FORMAL
IMP shinto religious_tradition FORMAL
IMP taoism religious_tradition FORMAL
IMP indigenous_traditions religious_tradition FORMAL

# Abrahamic sub-family
ATOM abrahamic_tradition 3 950
IMP abrahamic_tradition religious_tradition FORMAL
IMP judaism abrahamic_tradition EMPIRICAL
IMP christianity abrahamic_tradition EMPIRICAL
IMP islam abrahamic_tradition EMPIRICAL

# Dharmic sub-family
ATOM dharmic_tradition 3 950
IMP dharmic_tradition religious_tradition FORMAL
IMP hinduism dharmic_tradition EMPIRICAL
IMP buddhism dharmic_tradition EMPIRICAL
IMP jainism dharmic_tradition EMPIRICAL
IMP sikhism dharmic_tradition EMPIRICAL

# ============================================================================
# 3. Major sacred texts
# ============================================================================

ATOM bible 1 1000
ATOM quran 1 1000
ATOM torah 1 1000
ATOM tanakh 1 950
ATOM vedas 1 950
ATOM tripitaka 1 950
ATOM guru_granth_sahib 1 950
ATOM tao_te_ching 1 950
ATOM analects 1 950

IMP bible sacred_text FORMAL
IMP quran sacred_text FORMAL
IMP torah sacred_text FORMAL
IMP tanakh sacred_text FORMAL
IMP vedas sacred_text FORMAL
IMP tripitaka sacred_text FORMAL
IMP guru_granth_sahib sacred_text FORMAL
IMP tao_te_ching sacred_text FORMAL

IMP bible christianity EMPIRICAL
IMP quran islam EMPIRICAL
IMP torah judaism EMPIRICAL
IMP tanakh judaism EMPIRICAL
IMP vedas hinduism EMPIRICAL
IMP tripitaka buddhism EMPIRICAL
IMP guru_granth_sahib sikhism EMPIRICAL

# ============================================================================
# 4. Historical figures (well-documented + traditionally attributed)
# ============================================================================

ATOM jesus_of_nazareth 1 950
ATOM muhammad 1 950
ATOM siddhartha_gautama 1 950
ATOM moses 1 800
ATOM guru_nanak 1 950
ATOM baha_u_llah 1 950
ATOM confucius 1 950
ATOM zoroaster 1 850

IMP jesus_of_nazareth person FORMAL
IMP muhammad person FORMAL
IMP siddhartha_gautama person FORMAL
IMP guru_nanak person FORMAL
IMP baha_u_llah person FORMAL
IMP confucius person FORMAL

IMP jesus_of_nazareth christianity EMPIRICAL
IMP muhammad islam EMPIRICAL
IMP siddhartha_gautama buddhism EMPIRICAL
IMP guru_nanak sikhism EMPIRICAL
IMP baha_u_llah bahai_faith EMPIRICAL
IMP zoroaster zoroastrianism EMPIRICAL

# ============================================================================
# 5. Sacred places (well-documented geographical/historical sites)
# ============================================================================

ATOM jerusalem 1 1000
ATOM mecca 1 1000
ATOM medina 1 1000
ATOM bodh_gaya 1 950
ATOM varanasi 1 950
ATOM vatican_city 1 1000
ATOM amritsar 1 950
ATOM lumbini 1 900

IMP jerusalem sacred_place FORMAL
IMP mecca sacred_place FORMAL
IMP medina sacred_place FORMAL
IMP bodh_gaya sacred_place FORMAL
IMP varanasi sacred_place FORMAL
IMP vatican_city sacred_place FORMAL
IMP amritsar sacred_place FORMAL
IMP lumbini sacred_place FORMAL

# ============================================================================
# 6. Common religious practices (cross-tradition)
# ============================================================================

ATOM prayer 3 950
ATOM meditation 3 950
ATOM fasting 3 950
ATOM pilgrimage 3 950
ATOM scripture_recitation 3 900
ATOM alms_giving 3 900

IMP prayer religious_practice FORMAL
IMP meditation religious_practice FORMAL
IMP fasting religious_practice FORMAL
IMP pilgrimage religious_practice FORMAL
IMP scripture_recitation religious_practice FORMAL
IMP alms_giving religious_practice FORMAL

# ============================================================================
# 7. Well-documented historical dates
# ============================================================================

ATOM christianity_founded_1st_century 1 950
ATOM islam_founded_7th_century 1 950
ATOM buddhism_founded_5th_century_bce 1 900
ATOM protestant_reformation_1517 1 950
ATOM great_schism_1054 1 900

IMP christianity_founded_1st_century historical_event EMPIRICAL
IMP islam_founded_7th_century historical_event EMPIRICAL
IMP buddhism_founded_5th_century_bce historical_event EMPIRICAL
IMP protestant_reformation_1517 historical_event EMPIRICAL
IMP great_schism_1054 historical_event EMPIRICAL

ATOM historical_event 3 950

# ============================================================================
# 8. Cross-source citations
# ============================================================================

CITE src:pack:religion:v1 src:paper:doi:britannica-comparative-religion supports
CITE src:pack:religion:v1 src:paper:doi:oxford-handbook-of-religion supports
CITE src:pack:religion:v1 src:paper:doi:pew-research-global-religion-2020 supports
CITE src:pack:religion:v1 src:pack:world_history:v1 extends

# ============================================================================
# 9. Reinforcing observations for the highest-confidence claims
# ============================================================================

OBS christianity +1 1000
OBS islam +1 1000
OBS buddhism +1 1000
OBS bible +1 1000
OBS quran +1 1000
